# SYNTHETIC invalid fixture — not source data.
# why: printed text belongs to a printed face, not to the printing (smtg:intendedDomain of smtg:hasPrintedText). With rdfs:domain the reasoner would instead conclude that the printing IS a printed face, and since the two classes are disjoint the whole dataset would become inconsistent; SHACL reports the one misplaced triple.
# expect: The subject of smtg:hasPrintedText must be a smtg:PrintedFace
@prefix smtg: <https://w3id.org/smtg/ontology#> .
@prefix x: <https://w3id.org/smtg/id/synthetic/> .
x:p1 a smtg:CardPrinting ; smtg:hasPrintedText x:t1 .
x:t1 a smtg:PrintedName ; smtg:textValue "Fulmine"@it .
